      "id": "sol.amc-8-2008-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "After subdividing the central shaded square, the figure has \\(16\\) equal small squares.\n\nOf these, \\(6\\) are shaded and \\(10\\) are unshaded, so the desired ratio is \\(6:10=3:5\\).\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
